<title>ITALY: Italy Treasury starts Banco Napoli cap increase.</title>
<headline>Italy Treasury starts Banco Napoli cap increase.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian Treasury said on Tuesday it had kicked off a 1.977 trillion lire capital increase for troubled Banco di Napoli.</p>
<p>It said in a statement it had begun the underwriting for the operation, designed to recapitalise the ailing bank which the Treasury took control of after it unveiled record losses of 3.12 trillion lire in 1995 and increased its losses this year.</p>
<p>The Treasury is auctioning off a 60 percent stake in the bank, the biggest in southern Italy. Italian insurer INA said earlier it was preparing a bid together with state-controlled Banca Nazionale del Lavoro.</p>
</text>
